                    Design: I propose to integrate MixUp                        
                    augmentation (α=0.4) into the training                      
                    loop to improve generalization and                          
                    robustness across skin tones. For each                      
                    batch, we sample a mixing coefficient λ                     
                    from a Beta(α,α) distribution, shuffle                      
                    the batch, and linearly combine images                      
                    and labels accordingly. The loss is                         
                    computed as λ·L(model(mixed_imgs), y_a)                     
                    + (1−λ)·L(model(mixed_imgs), y_b). We                       
                    retain the existing                                         
                    WeightedRandomSampler for skin‐tone                         
                    fairness and TTA at validation and                          
                    inference, then rerun 5‐fold CV to                          
                    measure the AUROC improvement.                              
                    Code: import os                                             
                    import pandas as pd                                         
                    import numpy as np                                          
                    from PIL import Image                                       
