                    successfully without any errors. The                        
                    model used a ViT base architecture with                     
                    MixUp augmentation and a weighted                           
                    sampler to address skin tone fairness.                      
                    Cross-validation results show a strong                      
                    mean AUROC of approximately 0.937,                          
                    indicating good classification                              
                    performance. The approach appears                           
                    effective in balancing skin tone groups                     
                    via weighted sampling and MixUp                             
                    augmentation, contributing to fair                          
                    model training.                                             
