                    The model was trained using a ViT base                      
                    architecture with skin tone balancing                       
                    via a weighted sampler and mixup                            
                    augmentation. Cross-validation yielded                      
                    a strong mean AUROC of 0.9372,                              
                    indicating good discriminative                              
                    performance for malignancy                                  
                    classification. The final model was                         
                    retrained on the full dataset and saved                     
                    correctly. The prediction function uses                     
                    test-time augmentation for robust                           
                    inference. Overall, the approach                            
                    balances fairness and performance                           
                    effectively.                                                
                    Validation Metric: 0.9372                                   
                                                                                
                    -------------------------------                             
                    Design: I propose to enhance the                            
                    sampling strategy by combining                              
                    inverse‐frequency weights for both skin                     
                    tone groups and malignant vs benign                         
                    classes when creating the                                   
                    WeightedRandomSampler. This ensures                         
                    each batch is balanced across both skin                     
                    tone and lesion class distributions,                        
                    potentially improving overall                               
                    performance and fairness. We compute                        
                    per‐sample weights as the product of                        
                    inverse group frequency and inverse                         
                    class frequency, and apply this sampler                     
                    during cross‐validation and final                           
                    training. All other pipeline settings,                      
                    including TTA and model architecture,                       
                    remain unchanged.                                           
                    Code: import os                                             
                    import pandas as pd                                         
                    import numpy as np                                          
                    from PIL import Image                                       
                    import torch                                                
                    import torch.nn as nn                                       
                    import torch.optim as optim                                 
                    from torch.utils.data import Dataset,                       
                    DataLoader, WeightedRandomSampler                           
